# Files that control what CI runs, what it can reach and what gets signed (threat-model review 2026-10-25, TM-03, TM-13).
# With "Require review from Code Owners" on in the branch rule for main, a change here needs the owner's approval.
# docs/owner/cloudflare-setup.md ("Protect the main branch") says how to switch that on.
/.github/                        @UponAnonymous
/service/scripts/                @UponAnonymous
/build/                          @UponAnonymous
/tools/DbdPresence.ReleaseSigner/ @UponAnonymous
# The owner's local CI program runs with administrator rights on the owner's PC (local CI round 3, red-team M6): what it is built from, what tests it and
# the guide that says what it does are reviewed by the owner too.
/tools/DbdPresence.LocalCi/       @UponAnonymous
/tests/DbdPresence.LocalCi.Tests/ @UponAnonymous
/tests/DbdPresence.ArchitectureTests/LocalCiToolBoundaryTests*.cs @UponAnonymous
/docs/owner/free-ci.md            @UponAnonymous
# What the program is built with and what guards its rules (local CI round 4, red-team F11 and QA minor 1): the shared build files (a package or a setting added there is built
# into the program without appearing in its own project file), the tool versions, the compiler and style rules, the solution, and the whole architecture test project (its helpers
# and its project file decide what the boundary tests can see, not only the test files named above).
/Directory.Build.props            @UponAnonymous
/Directory.Build.targets          @UponAnonymous
/Directory.Packages.props         @UponAnonymous
/global.json                      @UponAnonymous
/nuget.config                     @UponAnonymous
/.config/                         @UponAnonymous
/.editorconfig                    @UponAnonymous
/DbdPresence.slnx                 @UponAnonymous
/tests/DbdPresence.ArchitectureTests/ @UponAnonymous
# These rules do nothing unless "Require review from Code Owners" is switched on in the branch rule for main. That is a repository setting this program cannot see: UNVERIFIED.
